<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_ThreeHeightFlora.xml — CRACKEDLANDS_THREE_HEIGHT_FLORA_1. Two of the canyon's three heights of flora (the third,
  the shade-line Veqma, is RM_Veqma.xml and carries its glow limit there). Mechanics: Source/RM_ThreeHeightFlora.cs.
  Neither is in the player's Plants menu (no sowTags); the laws hold for any spawn route anyway (CanEverPlantAt).
  Rulings 2026-10-09 (decision taken by question card): qirra mats yield dye; a talus clasp's pry opens fossil seams
  in natural walls with a letter, mining beside a clasp yields more, and cutting one sometimes turns up a fossil.
  Art: artpipe jobs RM_QirraMat / RM_TalusClasp (infrastructure/artpipe/art_lists/crackedlands_three_height_flora_2026-11-03.csv).
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RM_QirraMat</defName>
    <thingClass>RimMandrake.CrackedLands.RM_Plant_FloraLaw</thingClass>
    <label>qirra mat</label>
    <description>A flat red-brown mat that lies in canyon clay as a dry crust for years and opens only when a flood has wetted the ground — a spreading rosette of fleshy rust-maroon lobes, gone again as soon as the clay dries. Cut while open, its lobes give a strong red-brown dye.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RM_QirraMat</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>40</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.4</Flammability>
      <Nutrition>0.05</Nutrition>
      <Beauty>2</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <ingestible>
      <preferability>DesperateOnly</preferability>
    </ingestible>
    <plant>
      <fertilityMin>0.05</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0.2</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>1.5</growDays>
      <dieIfLeafless>true</dieIfLeafless>
      <neverBlightable>true</neverBlightable>
      <maxMeshCount>1</maxMeshCount>
      <topWindExposure>0</topWindExposure>
      <visualSizeRange>0.6~0.95</visualSizeRange>
      <harvestTag>Standard</harvestTag>
      <harvestedThingDef>Dye</harvestedThingDef>
      <harvestYield>2</harvestYield>
      <harvestWork>120</harvestWork>
      <wildOrder>1</wildOrder>
    </plant>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CrackedLands.RM_FloodWokenExtension" />
    </modExtensions>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RM_TalusClasp</defName>
    <thingClass>RimMandrake.CrackedLands.RM_Plant_TalusClasp</thingClass>
    <label>talus clasp</label>
    <description>A pale knot of chalk-white woody roots that grows only against bare canyon rock, its fingers wedged into the crevices. Over seasons the roots pry the crack wider until a face of the wall splits open, often on fossil-bearing strata. Rock mined beside a grown clasp comes away easier and richer, and cutting one now and then shakes loose a fossil from the crack it was working.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RM_TalusClasp</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>120</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.5</Flammability>
      <Beauty>1</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <ingestible>
      <preferability>NeverForNutrition</preferability>
    </ingestible>
    <plant>
      <fertilityMin>0</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>30</growDays>
      <dieIfLeafless>false</dieIfLeafless>
      <dieIfNoSunlight>false</dieIfNoSunlight>
      <neverBlightable>true</neverBlightable>
      <maxMeshCount>1</maxMeshCount>
      <topWindExposure>0.05</topWindExposure>
      <visualSizeRange>0.6~0.9</visualSizeRange>
      <!-- No harvest: owner ruling "stop giving wood" (plant economy rule E3, wood only from plants drawn 3.0+); a clasp is 0.9. -->
      <wildOrder>2</wildOrder>
    </plant>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CrackedLands.RM_WallRootedExtension">
        <fossilFindChance>0.15</fossilFindChance>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
